      en: "The Mausoleum of Hakim al-Termezi in Termiz, Uzbekistan, honors the Sufi scholar Muhammad ibn Ali al-Hakim al-Termezi, who lived in the 9th century. The building dates from the 15th century. The mausoleum has a dome and is decorated with blue tiles. It is a pilgrimage site for Muslims. The complex includes a mosque and a courtyard. Al-Termezi was a prominent hadith scholar. The tomb is flanked by a small minaret. The mausoleum was renovated in the 20th century.",
