      en: "The Ak-Saray Palace in Shahrisabz, Uzbekistan, was built starting in 1380 under Timur. It was a huge palace complex with an entrance portal 70 meters high. Today, only the remains of the portal stand. The palace was adorned with blue and gold tiles. Construction was never fully completed. The palace served as a ceremonial building. After Timur's decline, it fell into decay. The surviving portal height is about 38 meters. The palace is part of the old town of Shahrisabz, a UNESCO World Heritage site.",
